PALIMPSEST_TURN {"text":"## Delivered artifacts\n\nCreated and committed relative to `/run/fs-p/world`:\n\n- `study-plan.md`\n- `plan.json` — valid JSON; project `json-artifact` contract returned **supported**\n- `reviews/evidence.md`\n- `reviews/delivery.md`\n- `unresolved.md`\n\nWorkspace is clean; commits are local project revisions, not an approved ProjectIR promotion.\n\n## Plan in brief\n\n**Proposed primary configuration:** 3 × Reference, one per site.\n\n| Item | Cost |\n|---|---:|\n| 3 Reference units | 5,400 |\n| Required fixed costs | 1,280 |\n| S2 battery kit | 300 |\n| External logger | 0 |\n| **Total** | **6,980** |\n| Cap | 7,200 |\n| **Headroom** | **220** |\n\nThis is evidence-first: Reference is the only model with independent bench rows at high humidity (90–95% RH), and one model at all sites improves comparability. It is **not risk-free**: all three available Reference units are used, so there is no validated spare; a fourth Reference would cost 8,780 and exceed the cap.\n\nSchedule: 4-day lead + up to 3-day preparation + 14 observation days = 21 days. Under the plan’s conservative internal deadline of 2026-03-29 09:00 UTC, approval/order release is recommended by **2026-03-06** and is internally latest on **2026-03-08**. Less strict day-count readings allow about 2026-03-09, but that is not assumed.\n\n## Evidence standing\n\n- **Accepted for purpose:** R1–R6 and the 7,200 cap.\n- **Observed sources:** all six `sources/` files, hashed in `reviews/evidence.md`.\n- **Manufacturer claims:** Echo and Reference RH 20–95%, ±2 µg/m³; not accepted as independent field evidence.\n- **Independent bench observation:** only four rows per model. Echo covers RH 40–60% only, so **Echo at S2/S3 is brochure-only**. Reference covers 90/95% RH but sparsely; low-temperature and mid-high-humidity bands remain untested.\n- **Candidate conclusion:** the all-Reference plan is supported for planning, but R3 at S2/S3 is **not field-proven**.\n- **Open:** source acceptance, R5 approval, procurement approval, unit reservation, mounting/site access, battery/preparation power, and field-level uncertainty verification.\n\n## Independent subagent finding — separate and exploratory\n\nThe bounded audit is recorded as exploration `pje-baba1f6ddf0809b4e05c417006ac2b88`. It is **not accepted truth, Evidence, or approval**.\n\nIt agreed with the 6,980 arithmetic and the Echo high-humidity gap. It flagged:\n\n1. **S2 battery/preparation gap:** 3 preparation days + 14 observation days = up to 17 days of demand against a kit rated for 14 observation days.\n2. **Schedule boundary:** 2026-03-09 is possible under less strict day-count readings; the plan uses the stricter 2026-03-29 09:00 internal deadline.\n3. **Preparation scope:** the source does not say whether the 3 days are total or per site; per-site sequential would make the chain 27 days.\n4. **Sparse coverage:** S2 80–89% and S3 70–74%/76–89% RH are untested; high-RH rows are only 18–20 °C.\n5. Its “mean” figures are mean **absolute** deviations, not signed bias; signed biases are Echo +0.55 and Reference +0.225.\n\nThese flags are incorporated into the plan, delivery review, and `unresolved.md`.\n\n## Project mechanism state\n\n- Design task completed and is **VERIFYING**, awaiting operator acceptance/rework.\n- Journal records: candidate negative finding on Echo high-humidity evidence; open question on the no-spare risk; exploratory subagent finding; non-authoritative approval/procurement proposal.\n- Deterministic notes: budget **PASS**, schedule **PASS**, coverage **PASS**, source-identity **PASS**, approval **FAIL** (expected — no approval granted), `json-artifact` **supported**.\n- No source was accepted, no budget/procurement was approved, and no deployment was authorised.","toolCalls":["tool/call:bash","tool/result","tool/call:palimpsest_status","tool/result","tool/call:read","tool/result","tool/call:bash","tool/result","tool/call:bash","tool/result","tool/call:palimpsest_project",